      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since $X$ is paracompact, we may find a locally finite covering $\{  U'_{\alpha } \} _{\alpha \in A}$ of $X$, such that the each closure $\overline{ U'_{\alpha } }$ is contained in $U_{\alpha }$. Let $S$ denote the set of all subsets $A_0 \subseteq A$ having size $k+1$. For $A_0 \in S$, let $K(A_0) = \bigcap _{\alpha \in A_0} \overline{U_{\alpha }}$. Now set 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[ \widetilde{A} = \{  (\alpha , A_0, \beta ): \alpha \in A_0 \in S, \beta \in B(A_0) \}  \cup A. \]
</div>
    <p>
       For $\widetilde{\alpha } = (\alpha , A_0, \beta ) \in \widetilde{A}$, we set $\pi (\widetilde{\alpha }) = \alpha $ and 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[ W_{\widetilde{\alpha }} = (U'_{\alpha } - \bigcup _{\alpha \in A'_0 \in S} K(A'_0) ) \cup (V_{\beta } \cap U'_{\alpha }). \]
</div>
    <p>
       If $\alpha \in A \subseteq \widetilde{A}$, we let $\pi (\alpha ) = \alpha $ and $W_{\alpha } = U'_{\alpha } - \bigcup _{\alpha \in A_0 \in S} K(A_0)$. The local finiteness of the cover $\{  U'_{\alpha } \} $ ensures that each $W_{\widetilde{\alpha }}$ is an open set. It is now easy to check that the covering $\{  W_{ \widetilde{\alpha } } \} _{\widetilde{\alpha } \in \widetilde{A}}$ has the desired properties. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
